   "replay": {
    "doc": "Deadline replay of a song already played this set (scene-led deadline step 'repeat an earlier song in the scene'): the caller sets replay on the PickState and acceptCandidate then waives ONLY the played gate (playing, vetoed, language, length, scene, era all still apply). Never the song on air or any of the last min_gap played songs (the playing song counts as one).",
    "min_gap": 4
   },
   "scene_distance": {
    "doc": "HF13: under a pinned scene a candidate whose genre family is at most max_steps steps from the PINNED scene's family (never from the song now playing) on the genre graph passes the scene gate; closer is preferred (exact, then 1). VIBELOCK: max_steps is 1 (3 let hip hop reach pop, indie pop, disco house and reggaeton, so the set drifted), and vibe_bands add the mood band: when both the pinned scene and the candidate map to a band (mellow = romantic / wind-down, drive = party / energy) and share none, the candidate leaves the vibe; families in no band (pop, south_asian) never decide it. A caller judging against a moving reference (the playing song) passes scene_max_steps 1 so chained steps cannot drift. Graph = NEIGHBOUR_FAMILIES + extra_edges (sorted 'a|b' keys). hubs are generic labels: they may be an end of a path (adjacent to what they touch) but a path never passes through them, so 'electronic' or 'pop' never bridge two unrelated genres. Language is a separate hard gate and never follows genre distance.",
